# expo-updates code signing. The private key signs every OTA update: anyone
# holding it can push JavaScript to every install. Never commit it. Back it up
# somewhere durable (password manager), because losing it means no signed
# update can ever reach the shipped binary again without a new App Store build.
# certs/certificate.pem is public and IS committed — it gets embedded in the
# binary so the app can verify signatures. The `*.pem` rule above would
# otherwise swallow it, and EAS honours .gitignore when it uploads the project,
# so the build would silently ship with no certificate to verify against.
/keys/
!certs/certificate.pem

# Google Play service account. A private key that can upload builds, edit the
# store listing and read financial reports for com.actorrise.ghostlight. It is
# read off local disk by `eas submit` (eas.json -> submit.production.android),
# never bundled, so ignoring it costs nothing and committing it would hand
# anyone who clones this repo publishing rights to the app.
google-play-service-account.json
metro-file-map-expo-*

# EAS Build scratch dir. Left behind when a build is interrupted, and on the
# next run its presence breaks the upload: eas tries to copy the project into
# a subdirectory of itself.
eas-cli-nodejs/

# Generated growth assets. The SVG + caption for each card is small, text, and worth
# keeping as an archive of what has already been posted; the PNG renders are not.
content/cards/*.png
